        "problem": "Compute $\\text{E}[-6X-1]$ if $\\text{E}[X]=-\\frac{3}{2}.$",
        "worked_solution": "For any constants $a$ and $b$ and any random variable $X,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[aX+b]=a\\text{E}[X]+b.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[-6X-1] & =-6\\text{E}[X]-1 \\\\  & =-6(-\\frac{3}{2})-1 \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
