        "knowledge_point": "Finding Mixed Second-Order Partial Derivatives",
        "problem": "For the function $f(x,y),$ calculate $\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}$ given that $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=\\frac{3{y}^{2}}{{x}^{3}+{y}^{3}}.$",
        "worked_solution": "To find $\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}$ we differentiate the given first-order partial derivative $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\frac{∂f}{∂y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\frac{3{y}^{2}}{{x}^{3}+{y}^{3}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{6y({x}^{3}+{y}^{3})-3{y}^{2}(3{y}^{2})}{{({x}^{3}+{y}^{3})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6y{x}^{3}+6{y}^{4}-9{y}^{4}}{{({x}^{3}+{y}^{3})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6y{x}^{3}-3{y}^{4}}{{({x}^{3}+{y}^{3})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3y(2{x}^{3}-{y}^{3})}{{({x}^{3}+{y}^{3})}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
